      "text": "Error handlers are tools in Make that allow you to deal with errors or unexpected events in your scenario . An error handler is connected to a module and is the last module of the error handling route. When the module outputs an error, the error handler prevents the scenario from stopping . Instead, it intercepts the error and executes the scenario based on the error handler’s configuration.",
